{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":23.68000030517578,"text":"A thin sheet of gold, hammered until it took the shape of a face, laid over a dead king at Mycenae. Heinrich Schliemann found it in 1876 and believed he was holding the face of Agamemnon, the king from the Iliad. He was wrong, and the mistake is useful. The mask is roughly 300 years older than the time the Trojan Wars placed in. The name stuck anyway.","words":[{"word":"A","start":0,"end":0.4399999976158142},{"word":"thin","start":0.4399999976158142,"end":0.6800000071525574},{"word":"sheet","start":0.6800000071525574,"end":0.8600000143051147},{"word":"of","start":0.8600000143051147,"end":1.4800000190734863},{"word":"gold","start":1.4800000190734863,"end":1.4800000190734863},{"word":"hammered","start":1.9600000381469727,"end":2.180000066757202},{"word":"until","start":2.180000066757202,"end":2.319999933242798},{"word":"it","start":2.319999933242798,"end":2.640000104904175},{"word":"took","start":2.640000104904175,"end":2.640000104904175},{"word":"the","start":2.640000104904175,"end":2.9800000190734863},{"word":"shape","start":2.9800000190734863,"end":2.9800000190734863},{"word":"of","start":2.9800000190734863,"end":3.180000066757202},{"word":"a","start":3.180000066757202,"end":3.640000104904175},{"word":"face","start":3.640000104904175,"end":3.640000104904175},{"word":"laid","start":4.159999847412109,"end":4.380000114440918},{"word":"over","start":4.380000114440918,"end":4.699999809265137},{"word":"a","start":4.699999809265137,"end":4.980000019073486},{"word":"dead","start":4.980000019073486,"end":5.179999828338623},{"word":"king","start":5.179999828338623,"end":5.480000019073486},{"word":"at","start":5.480000019073486,"end":5.860000133514404},{"word":"Mycenae","start":5.860000133514404,"end":6.300000190734863},{"word":"Heinrich","start":7.019999980926514,"end":7.239999771118164},{"word":"Schliemann","start":7.239999771118164,"end":7.639999866485596},{"word":"found","start":7.6399998664855